  "id": "health-psychology",
  "term": "health psychology",
  "definition": "Health psychology is the area of psychology that studies how psychological, biological-behavioural, and environmental factors work together to affect physical and mental health, wellbeing, and illness. It uses a biopsychosocial view to understand how everyday behaviours and contexts can help or harm emotional, cognitive, and social functioning.",
